# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run artifacts. THIS IS A SECURITY BOUNDARY, not just noise reduction.
#
# A run folder contains a HAR of an authenticated session: Authorization
# headers, Cookie/Set-Cookie, request bodies, plus screenshots of a logged-in
# application. The observer redacts known secret headers on capture (see
# src/observer/redact.ts), but redaction is a best-effort net over an unbounded
# space of app-specific tokens — it is not a licence to commit these.
#
# Never remove these two lines. Never `git add -f` a run folder.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reporting/
.vault/

# Local target config — contains staging URLs and, depending on how you wire
# it, credential references. The .example file is the tracked template.
shakeout.config.ts
!shakeout.config.example.ts
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output / deps
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
